## Question 9

Ridership as a function of population and jobs within a half mile, terminal status, and airport connection.

```{r}
#| label: q9-lm
m1 <- lm(rider ~ pop_halfmile + jobs_halfmile + terminal_d + airport_d, data = hrt)
summary(m1)
```

```{r}
#| label: q9-helpers
#| echo: false 
cf1 <- summary(m1)$coefficients
dirn <- function(x) ifelse(x > 0, "positive", "negative")
sig  <- function(tbl, v) paste0("p ", ifelse(tbl[v, 4] < 0.001, "< 0.001", paste0("= ", signif(tbl[v, 4], 2))),
                                ifelse(tbl[v, 4] < 0.05, ", statistically significant", ", not statistically significant"),
                                " at the 5% level")
```

```{r}
#| output: asis
#| echo: false
cat(glue::glue(r"---(The model explains <<round(100*summary(m1)$r.squared, 1)>>% of the variation in station ridership (adjusted R² = <<round(summary(m1)$adj.r.squared, 3)>>). Holding the other variables constant, each coefficient is the change in average daily station ridership (riders) for a one-unit change in the predictor:)---", .open = "<<", .close = ">>"), "\n\n")
```

```{r}
#| output: asis
#| echo: false
cat(glue::glue(r"---(- **Population within a half mile:** the relationship is <<dirn(cf1["pop_halfmile",1])>>. Each additional resident is associated with <<round(cf1["pop_halfmile",1], 3)>> additional daily riders, or about <<round(1000*cf1["pop_halfmile",1])>> more riders for every 1,000 additional residents (<<sig(cf1, "pop_halfmile")>>).
- **Jobs within a half mile:** the relationship is <<dirn(cf1["jobs_halfmile",1])>>. Each additional job is associated with <<round(cf1["jobs_halfmile",1], 3)>> additional daily riders, or about <<round(1000*cf1["jobs_halfmile",1])>> more riders for every 1,000 additional jobs (<<sig(cf1, "jobs_halfmile")>>).
- **Terminal station:** the relationship is <<dirn(cf1["terminal_d",1])>>. Terminal stations have on average <<round(abs(cf1["terminal_d",1]))>> <<ifelse(cf1["terminal_d",1] > 0, "more", "fewer")>> daily riders than non-terminal stations with the same population and jobs (<<sig(cf1, "terminal_d")>>).
- **Airport connection:** the relationship is <<dirn(cf1["airport_d",1])>>. Stations connecting to an airport have on average <<round(abs(cf1["airport_d",1]))>> <<ifelse(cf1["airport_d",1] > 0, "more", "fewer")>> daily riders than other stations with the same population and jobs (<<sig(cf1, "airport_d")>>).)---", .open = "<<", .close = ">>"), "\n\n")
```

The indicator coefficients are in riders and are not comparable in size with the per-person and per-job coefficients, because they are measured in different units. Population and jobs are the continuous predictors, so their effects scale with how many residents and jobs a station has nearby.

